**Date:** 30 October 2026 · **Deciders:** support desk · **Replaces:** [0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)

## Context

Decision 0001 merged reports whose subject lines matched. #4471 shows what that costs: 412 reports with
12 different subjects ended up in one ticket marked known, and they hold three problems with three fixes
([#4471 is three problems, not one](/kb/incidents/4471-split)). People describe different bugs in the same words.

## Decision

Two reports are the same issue when they have the same **cause**, worked out from the tenant (its locale and
booking form) and the channel, as `causeOf` in `src/lib/kb/causes.ts` does. A report whose body shows a
different mechanism (a one-day move, not a swap) goes to its own ticket even when its tenant points elsewhere.
The subject line and the intake tag are hints, never the key.

Each ticket a big ticket is split into is listed in `src/lib/data/tickets.json`, so the incident page
shows where every cause is tracked.

## Consequences

- Triage reads the tenant and the channel, not just the subject. Slower on an incident morning.
- A queued fix closes only its own cause's ticket. The rest stay open.
- 0001 stays as written; this record replaces it.

